docs/design/dao.space.v0.md:31:Concretely, a DaoSpace is **a collection of file-backed dao.streams**. `dao.space/open!` returns a **handle** to that collection; the handle plays two roles. As a **factory**, it opens member write logs — `ds/open!` delegates through the space to realize a `dao.stream.file` member, and `ds/append!` appends datom frames to it. As a **read target**, the handle answers questions over *all* member logs at once: `dao.space/q` (Datalog) and `dao.space/match` (datom pattern). The asymmetry is deliberate — **writing is streaming, reading is querying.** You never read the space *as* a stream; member streams carry datoms in, the space answers questions out.
